# A Clone can't become a copy of Humility while Humility applies to it: Clone's "You may have this creature enter as a copy
# of any creature" is its own replacement effect, judged on Clone as it would exist on the battlefield, continuous effects
# that already exist included (CR 614.12) - and there it is a creature that Humility strips. Opalescence (turn 1) makes
# Humility (turn 3) a creature, so Humility takes its own ability too; its effect goes on applying, to itself and to every
# other creature, entering ones included (CR 613.6). So on turn 5 Clone is offered nothing to copy - not the animated
# Humility, not anything (the refusal "! Bot1.Accept" holds) - and enters as itself, a Shapeshifter that Humility makes 1/1.
# Humility, its own 7b part after Opalescence's 4/4, is 1/1 too.

